  "goodToKnow": "Der Zentner is an old unit of weight: in Germany 50 kilograms (100 Pfund of 500 grams), while in Austria and Switzerland it's 100 kilograms. It's still used informally in farming and in idioms: zentnerschwer means extremely heavy, as in Mir fiel ein zentnerschwerer Stein vom Herzen (a huge weight was lifted from my mind). From Latin centenarius (of a hundred). The plural is the same."
